## What to build:

### 1. TurnTimeline (left panel)

Vertical list of turns with selection.

```typescript
@Component({ selector: "tfc-turn-timeline" })
export class TurnTimeline {
  turns = input.required<TurnDefinition[]>();
  selectedIndex = input<number>(0);
  onSelect = output<number>();
  onAdd = output<void>();
  onDuplicate = output<number>();
  onDelete = output<number>();
}
```

Template — for each turn:
- Turn index badge (0, 1, 2...)
- Title (truncated ~20 chars), or "Turn N" if no title
- Stress pip: small colored dot — green for base_stress_delta=0, amber for >0, blue for <0
- Selected state: highlighted with `background: var(--color-muted)`
- Click → emits onSelect with turn_index
- Small action buttons: duplicate icon, delete icon (use text "Dup" / "Del" if no icon component)

"+ Add Turn" button at bottom of the list.

Style: fixed width ~14rem, full height, border-right, overflow-y auto.

### 2. TurnInjectEditor

Edits the injects for a single turn.

```typescript
@Component({ selector: "tfc-turn-inject-editor" })
export class TurnInjectEditor {
  injects = input.required<TurnInjectDef[]>();
  roles = input.required<{ id: string; label: string }[]>();
  turnIndex = input.required<number>();
}
```

Inject this component's parent store: `ScenarioBuilderStore`.

For each inject:
- Role badge(s) showing target_roles, or "All" if empty
- Textarea with inject text
- Delete button
- Role selector: checkboxes or multi-select of available roles

"+ Add Inject" button: creates a new `TurnInjectDef` with empty text and `target_roles: []`.

All mutations go through store: `addInjectToTurn`, `removeInjectFromTurn`, `updateInjectInTurn`.

### 3. TurnCardPicker

Selects which blue cards are available this turn and configures per-turn scoring.

```typescript
@Component({ selector: "tfc-turn-card-picker" })
export class TurnCardPicker {
  catalog = input.required<BlueCardDef[]>();
  selectedCards = input.required<TurnCardConfig[]>();
  turnIndex = input.required<number>();
  maxSelections = input(2);
}
```

Inject `ScenarioBuilderStore`.

Template:
- Max selections input at top: `<input type="number" [value]="maxSelections()">`
- For each card in catalog:
  - Checkbox: checked if card_id is in selectedCards
  - Card ID badge + title
  - If checked, expandable config row with:
    - Score: number input
    - Stress delta: number input
    - "Targets system" badge (read-only, from catalog)
  - Keep system/domain effects simple for now — just the score and stress fields. Effects editing can be deferred.
- "Card not in catalog?" link: `<a routerLink="/foundation" class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Edit Foundation →</a>`

On checkbox toggle: call `store.addCardToTurn` or `store.removeCardFromTurn`.
On score/stress change: call `store.updateCardInTurn`.

### 4. TurnEditor (right panel)

The full editing form for a single turn.

```typescript
@Component({ selector: "tfc-turn-editor" })
export class TurnEditor {
  turn = input.required<TurnDefinition>();
  turnIndex = input.required<number>();
  catalog = input.required<BlueCardDef[]>();
  roles = input.required<{ id: string; label: string }[]>();
}
```

Inject `ScenarioBuilderStore`.

Template — 5 sections using `<ui-card>`:

**Section 1: Turn Header**
```html
<ui-card title="Turn Header">
  <div class="flex items-center gap-sm">
    <span class="badge">Turn {{ turnIndex() }}</span>
  </div>
  <input class="input-base" placeholder="Turn title" [value]="turn().title" (change)="updateTitle($event)" />
  <textarea class="input-base" rows="3" placeholder="Facilitator prompt..." [value]="turn().facilitator_prompt ?? ''" (input)="updatePrompt($event)"></textarea>
  <label class="flex items-center gap-xs text-sm">
    <input type="checkbox" [checked]="turn().has_decisions" (change)="toggleDecisions($event)" />
    Has decisions
  </label>
  @if (!turn().has_decisions) {
    <input type="number" class="input-base" placeholder="Duration (ms)" [value]="turn().duration_ms ?? ''" (change)="updateDuration($event)" />
  }
</ui-card>
```

**Section 2: Injects**
```html
<ui-card title="Injects">
  <tfc-turn-inject-editor [injects]="turn().injects" [roles]="roles()" [turnIndex]="turnIndex()" />
</ui-card>
```

**Section 3: Blue Cards** (hidden when !has_decisions)
```html
@if (turn().has_decisions) {
  <ui-card title="Blue Cards">
    <tfc-turn-card-picker
      [catalog]="catalog()"
      [selectedCards]="turn().available_cards"
      [turnIndex]="turnIndex()"
      [maxSelections]="turn().max_selections"
    />
  </ui-card>
}
```

**Section 4: Turn Consequences**
```html
<ui-card title="Turn Consequences">
  <div class="flex items-center gap-sm">
    <span class="text-sm">Base stress delta:</span>
    <input type="number" class="input-base" style="width: 5rem" [value]="turn().base_stress_delta" (change)="updateStressDelta($event)" />
  </div>
  <!-- System/domain effects on start: defer complex editors, show as JSON or simple text for now -->
</ui-card>
```

**Section 5: Facilitator Notes** (collapsible)
```html
<ui-card title="Facilitator Notes">
  <textarea class="input-base" rows="2" placeholder="Best path notes..." [value]="turn().best_path?.notes ?? ''" (input)="updateBestPathNotes($event)"></textarea>
  <textarea class="input-base" rows="2" placeholder="Acceptable path notes..." [value]="turn().acceptable_path?.notes ?? ''" (input)="updateAcceptablePathNotes($event)"></textarea>
  <textarea class="input-base" rows="2" placeholder="Design notes..." [value]="turn().design_notes" (input)="updateDesignNotes($event)"></textarea>
</ui-card>
```

All updates delegate to `store.updateTurn(turnIndex, { ... })`.

### 5. ScenarioTurnsTab (orchestrator)

Split layout with timeline left and editor right.

```typescript
@Component({ selector: "tfc-scenario-turns-tab" })
export class ScenarioTurnsTab implements OnInit {
  store = inject(ScenarioBuilderStore);
  private domainApi = inject(DomainConfigApiService);

  selectedTurnIndex = signal(0);
  catalog = signal<BlueCardDef[]>([]);
  roles = signal<{ id: string; label: string }[]>([]);

  selectedTurn = computed(() => {
    const turns = this.store.content().turns ?? [];
    return turns.find(t => t.turn_index === this.selectedTurnIndex()) ?? null;
  });

  ngOnInit() {
    // Load DomainConfig for catalog and roles
    this.domainApi.getBySlug("silent-wake").subscribe(config => {
      this.catalog.set(config.blue_card_catalog);
      this.roles.set(config.roles);
    });
    // Auto-create Turn 0 if no turns exist
    const turns = this.store.content().turns ?? [];
    if (turns.length === 0) {
      this.store.addTurn({
        turn_index: 0, title: "Pre-Sail Briefing", has_decisions: false,
        facilitator_prompt: null, duration_ms: 900000,
        inject_ids: [], decision_template_id: null,
        injects: [], available_cards: [], max_selections: 2,
        base_stress_delta: 0, system_effects_on_start: [],
        domain_effects_on_start: [], best_path: null,
        acceptable_path: null, design_notes: "",
      });
    }
  }
}
```

Template:
```html
<div class="flex" style="height: 100%">
  <tfc-turn-timeline
    style="width: 14rem; border-right: 1px solid var(--color-border); overflow-y: auto; flex-shrink: 0"
    [turns]="store.content().turns ?? []"
    [selectedIndex]="selectedTurnIndex()"
    (onSelect)="selectedTurnIndex.set($event)"
    (onAdd)="addTurn()"
    (onDuplicate)="store.duplicateTurn($event)"
    (onDelete)="deleteTurn($event)"
  />
  <div style="flex: 1; overflow-y: auto; padding: var(--spacing-lg)">
    @if (selectedTurn(); as turn) {
      <tfc-turn-editor
        [turn]="turn"
        [turnIndex]="selectedTurnIndex()"
        [catalog]="catalog()"
        [roles]="roles()"
      />
    } @else {
      <p class="text-muted-foreground p-lg">Select or add a turn to begin editing.</p>
    }
  </div>
</div>
```

### 6. Wire into builder view

In `scenario-builder-view.ts`, replace the turns placeholder:

```html
@if (viewMode() === "turns") {
  <tfc-scenario-turns-tab />
}
```

The turns tab does NOT use the sidebar layout — it has its own split panel. When on the turns tab, the builder's sidebar should still show (existing scenarios list is still useful).

## Context

Read these files to understand patterns:
- `apps/tfc/frontend/src/app/features/scenario-builder/scenario-builder.store.ts` — store with turn CRUD methods (addTurn, removeTurn, updateTurn, duplicateTurn, addInjectToTurn, etc.)
- `apps/tfc/frontend/src/app/features/scenario-builder/domain/turn-mutations.ts` — pure mutation functions
- `apps/tfc/frontend/src/app/features/scenario-builder/scenario-event-editor.ts` — existing editor pattern
- `apps/tfc/frontend/src/app/core/scenario-api.service.ts` — TurnDefinition, TurnInjectDef, TurnCardConfig types
- `apps/tfc/frontend/src/app/core/domain-config-api.service.ts` — BlueCardDef, DomainRole types

**IMPORTANT constraints:**
- Each file must be under 350 lines
- Use OnPush change detection
- Use signals, not RxJS observables for local state
- CSS: use existing utility classes, no new CSS files needed
- Import `CardComponent`, `ButtonDirective`, `BadgeComponent` from `@aspect/ui`
- All mutations through the store, not directly manipulating arrays

## Your Job

1. Read existing patterns
2. Create all 5 components
3. Wire into builder view
4. Verify `ng build` passes
5. Commit
6. Self-review and report

